  (section
    (heading "Implementation Notes")
    (subsection
      (heading "SDTS Issue #2: Rate Limiter Default (CRITICAL)")
      (para "**Problem:** Swift v1.0.2 used 100 req/60s, Python used 10,000 req/60s")
      (para "**Impact:** High-frequency trading systems were blocked by Swift")
      (para "**Solution:**")
      (item "1. Default MUST be 10,000 in initializer")
      (item "2. Warning logged if overridden to value < 10,000")
      (item "3. Unit test validates default is 10,000")
      (item "4. Documentation explains rationale")
      (para "**Code validation:**")
      (code "init(maxRequests: Int = 10_000, windowSeconds: TimeInterval = 60.0) {
    // CRITICAL: Default is 10,000 for HFT compatibility")
      (para "**Test validation:**")
      (code "func testDefaultIs10000() async {
    let rl = RateLimiter()
    let config = await rl.getConfig()
    XCTAssertEqual(config.maxRequests, 10_000)
}"))
    (subsection
      (heading "SDTS Issue #3: Replay Protection")
      (para "**Problem:** Python implementation lacked replay protection")
      (para "**Impact:** Security vulnerability - replay attacks possible")
      (para "**Solution:**")
      (item "Implement nonce cache with expiry")
      (item "Check all incoming packets for duplicate nonces")
      (item "Automatic cleanup to prevent memory exhaustion"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Actor Safety")
      (para "All three classes are actors:")
      (item "**ReplayProtection:** Thread-safe nonce tracking")
      (item "**RateLimiter:** Thread-safe per-peer counters")
      (item "**KeyStore:** Thread-safe key management")
      (para "This prevents race conditions in concurrent environments."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Performance Considerations")
      (para "**Replay Protection:**")
      (item "O(1) lookup using dictionary")
      (item "Periodic cleanup (every 100 checks)")
      (item "Memory bounded by (rate × expiry time)")
      (para "**Rate Limiter:**")
      (item "O(1) lookup per peer")
      (item "O(n) cleanup per check (n = requests in window)")
      (item "Memory: ~10,000 timestamps × 8 bytes = 80 KB per peer max")
      (para "**KeyStore:**")
      (item "O(1) lookup per peer")
      (item "Minimal memory overhead")))
